/S /P
/P 91 0 R
/E (Our robot can stockpile catalysts by launching them across the field and use a ground intake to gain full catalyst control in under 15 seconds)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
112 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 91 0 R
/T (Finally, for our strategy to work, we realized that a large extending hopper that could store 100+ particles to allow for sweeps through the middle to parallelize catalysts and scoring particles. We considered other design additions such as swerve, an ascent mechanism, and dual sided intakes, but came to the conclusion that they required too many actuators or added unnecessary complexity as our paths were relatively straight and scored thousands of points.)
/E (Finally, for our strategy to work, we realized that a large extending hopper that could store 100+ particles to allow for sweeps through the middle to parallelize catalysts and scoring particles. We considered other design additions such as swerve, an ascent mechanism, and dual sided intakes, but came to the conclusion that they required too many actuators or added unnecessary complexity as our paths were relatively straight and scored thousands of points.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [9]
>>
